<https://cair-nepal.org/heritagegraph/yearOffsetFromGregorian> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Number of years this calendar runs ahead of the Gregorian (Common Era) year at the start of its year (e.g. 57 for Bikram Sambat, -879 for Nepal Sambat). Because the calendar's new year does not fall on 1 January (see hg:epochDateGregorian), a year-precision date Y converts to the two-year interval [Y - offset, Y - offset + 1] CE; the single year Y - offset is correct only for dates between the calendar's new year and 31 December. A calendar whose new year is 1 January converts to Y - offset exactly."@en .
